# Defects planted in a copy of one source of src/css, one edit a line (the lines of one name are the edits of one defect):
#
#   <name> TAB <file in src/css> TAB <old text> TAB <new text>
#
# The old text is literal (a `\n` in it is a line feed) and must be in the file exactly once. One defect for each layer the computed-style call stands on:
# the units of the values engine, the simplification of a calculation, the channels of a color, an inherited flag, the distribution of a shorthand, the
# order of the sort criteria of the cascade, the used color scheme of `normal`, `display: contents` on an SVG element, the separator of a dash array, the budget of substitution, the specificity a presentation attribute is given, and the sort order of the dump.
#
# Two gates see them, each with the unedited library as its control:
#   * `make check-css-grammar-plants` (tools/css/plant-grammar.py, part of `make test`) builds the library with the edit and runs tests/test-css-style.cpp:
#     it must fail (the plants appear there as `style-<name>`);
#   * `tools/oracle/run-css-style-oracle.sh --controls` (all but the sort criterion, the budget, the specificity of a presentation attribute and the dump order, which the population is below) asks the browsers' recorded answers of the population again of the edited library: the differential
#     must fail (exit 3: an unlisted divergence, a count that is not the listed one, a witness or a control that does not hold).
